# Corpus unit fre/C03 — gap (generalization; benchmark_evaluation)
#
# Source: m0/annotations/fre.yaml C03 (generalization; corpus pin 62e9b54). Headline: a single
# frozen FRE-all agent beats GC-IQL/GC-BC on non-goal-reaching families (ant-directional 55.2 vs
# 4.8/6.5; kitchen 66 vs 3/1) while staying competitive on goal-reaching (ant-goal 48.8 vs 0.0).
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * Family map: benchmark_evaluation. S = fre_all, B = gc_baselines (GC-IQL/GC-BC),
#     Q = cross_family_return. Per-family cells live in `nl` and refs.
#   * The annotation's mandatory CQ2 is unmet-gap: the conditioning protocol for the goal-
#     conditioned baselines on non-goal tasks (directional, simplex, path) is never stated, so
#     their near-zero scores could be partly a task-specification artifact. Mapped onto
#     policy-mandatory benchmark_valid (is the benchmark valid for the comparands?) -> unmet. The
#     benchmark_evaluation argument is declared as a located hole with `open benchmark_valid`
#     (lowering re-done for issue #15 under lara-core@0.3; until lara-core@0.2 the open mandatory
#     obligation rejected the unit, so the arg was omitted): it is not an AF node and the claim
#     stays gap on empty complete support.
#   * CQ1 (one frozen FRE-all checkpoint across every family, no per-family specialists)
#     discharges protocol_fixed on the hole. The optional environment_match has no annotated basis
#     and is opened (R5 question accounting; no status effect). The optional variance CQ3 (met,
#     mean +- std) has no benchmark_evaluation question and is omitted (no status effect).
#   * The path-task tension (GC-IQL scores 46.6/70.3 on ant-path, above FRE) is internal to the
#     artifact's own table, not a dead-end node with decision=undercut, so per the annotation it
#     surfaces as this header note, not an attack edge.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact fre at sha256:c1bb86743873
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim, stated but not assemblable at corpus-v1's evidential bar --------------

claim c03
  nl      = "A single frozen FRE-all agent beats GC-IQL/GC-BC on non-goal-reaching families (ant-directional 55.2 vs 4.8/6.5; kitchen 66 vs 3/1) while staying competitive on goal-reaching (ant-goal 48.8 vs 0.0); the GC conditioning protocol on non-goal tasks is unspecified"
  formal  = performs(fre_all, gc_baselines, cross_family_return)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = unreviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves are present ... ------------------------------------------------------------

leaf e1 : reports(e01, benchmark_result(fre_all, gc_baselines, cross_family_return, positive))
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [evidence/tables/table1_main_results.md, Table-1-row-ant-directional, Table-1-row-kitchen]

leaf e2 : fixed_protocol(fre_all, gc_baselines, e01)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E01-Procedure-steps-2-5]

# --- ... but only an incomplete argument (a located hole) is declarable -------------------------

# The incomplete argument: benchmark_valid has no honest leaf — the GC baselines' conditioning
# protocol on non-goal tasks is unspecified — and corpus-v1 makes it mandatory, so a1 is a hole.
arg a1 : supports(c03) by benchmark_evaluation(fre_all, gc_baselines, cross_family_return, e01)
  discharge protocol_fixed    with e2
  open      benchmark_valid
  open      environment_match

status c03

# ==============================================================================================
# EXPECTED VERDICT (golden oracle)
# ==============================================================================================
# Compiled AF: no arguments (a1 is a located hole, not an AF node).
# Located hole: a1 (benchmark_evaluation), open obligations [benchmark_valid]; sources no attacks.
# Claim status:
#   c03 -> gap (empty complete support; statusC = Gap iff null claimSupport, spec §8;
#          the hole a1 is reported in the verdict's holes section, not as a node)
